# Persist an explicit viewer pin from Auto and observe the resulting content
# respawn. Auto currently routes to genet.livery; the retired genet.web lane is
# no longer registered. The Inspector lowers SetViewerOverride, the sidecar
# persists it, and the restart twin verifies the saved pin. Network-dependent
# (example.com); use a fresh profile and reuse it for the restore twin.
settle 30
key escape

open https://example.com/
settle 30
act Toggle live content
settle 30
assert content-live

# Auto currently resolves to the registered livery lane.
act Open Inspector pane
settle 5
assert row Engine: genet.livery
assert row Viewer: auto

# Pin the currently selected lane explicitly. The radio list is collapsed by
# default, so expose it before selecting the livery option.
act Open Inspector pane
settle 5
assert pane inspector
click surface:inspector role:button Change viewer
settle 2
click-row genet.livery
settle 30
assert event viewer-changed
assert content-live
assert row Viewer: genet.livery
assert row Engine: genet.livery
# The livery lane reports structure through the trait now (genet
# 8e7524f41c4) — the respawned session's facts carry the real title, no
# more "none for this lane".
assert row Document title: Example Domain
capture 01_livery_applied

log settings row (viewer applied via pinned respawn) complete
